<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/21st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">2018 Armenian revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2018">2018</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a> · Also known as Armenian Velvet Revolution</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The 2018 Armenian revolution, also called the Velvet Revolution, was a wave of peaceful protests in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> in April and May 2018. It began against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serzh-sargsyan">Serzh Sargsyan</a>'s move from president to prime minister under a new parliamentary constitution and forced his resignation within a week. The protest leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikol-pashinyan">Nikol Pashinyan</a> was elected prime minister by parliament on 8 May 2018.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/2018-armenian-revolution.jpg" alt="2018 Armenian revolution" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: RaffiKojian · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:April_22_yerevan_republic_square_protest.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
